Exercise 1: Simple CRUD Application
Create a console-based Employee Management System with:
• Add employee
• View all employees
• Update employee salary
• Delete employee
• Search employee by name

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create Database mysql_jdbc_db;

USE mysql_jdbc_db;

CREATE TABLE employee(
   empId INT PRIMARY KEY,
   name VARCHAR(50),
   salary DOUBLE
);


1.Add Employee:-

INSERT INTO employee(empId, name, salary) 
VALUES
(101,'Vikash',970000),
(102,'Vishal',89000),
(103,'Anuj',90000),
(104,'Anupam',88000),
(105,'Virendra',70000);

Output:

3	9	16:39:23	INSERT INTO employee(empId, name, salary) 
 VALUES
 (101,'Vikash',970000),
 (102,'Vishal',89000),
 (103,'Anuj',90000),
 (104,'Anupam',88000),
 (105,'Virendra',70000)	5 row(s) affected
 Records: 5  Duplicates: 0  Warnings: 0	0.000 sec
 
2.View All Employee:-

   SELECT *FROM employee;
   
   
   Output:-
   
+-------+----------+--------+
| empId | name     | salary |
+-------+----------+--------+
|   101 | Vikash   | 970000 |
|   102 | Vishal   |  89000 |
|   103 | Anuj     |  90000 |
|   104 | Anupam   |  88000 |
|   105 | Virendra |  70000 |
